WEBVTT

00:01:29.235 --> 00:01:30.773
I decided to find out.

00:01:32.362 --> 00:01:35.471
What I quickly learned
is that we don't know very much.

00:01:35.495 --> 00:01:38.621
The first reason is just
how vast oceans are,

00:01:38.645 --> 00:01:40.986
covering 70 percent of the planet,

00:01:41.010 --> 00:01:44.555
and yet we know they drive
complex planetary systems

00:01:44.579 --> 00:01:45.759
like global weather,

00:01:45.783 --> 00:01:48.228
which affect all of us on a daily basis,

00:01:48.252 --> 00:01:49.870
sometimes dramatically.

00:01:50.562 --> 00:01:53.746
And yet, those activities
are mostly invisible to us.

00:01:54.944 --> 00:01:58.709
Ocean data is scarce by any standard.

00:01:59.268 --> 00:02:04.372
Back on land, I had grown used to
accessing lots of sensors --